WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.513
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online Advanced.

2
00:00:05.813 --> 00:00:09.037
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.337 --> 00:00:18.270
Unit forty-nine: Innovation in Agriculture. In this unit, you will discuss how technology can transform farming.

4
00:00:19.283 --> 00:00:20.958
precision agriculture.

5
00:00:21.658 --> 00:00:28.696
precision agriculture means farming that uses data and sensors to apply exactly what crops need.

6
00:00:28.996 --> 00:00:32.726
Precision agriculture reduces fertiliser waste.

7
00:00:33.426 --> 00:00:37.854
Your turn. Say: precision agriculture.

8
00:00:40.554 --> 00:00:42.066
precision agriculture.

9
00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:44.527
drip irrigation.

10
00:00:45.227 --> 00:00:50.675
drip irrigation means watering plants slowly through small tubes at their roots.

11
00:00:50.975 --> 00:00:53.659
Drip irrigation saves up to half the water.

12
00:00:54.359 --> 00:00:57.592
Your turn. Say: drip irrigation.

13
00:01:00.292 --> 00:01:01.560
drip irrigation.

14
00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:04.108
climate-smart farming.

15
00:01:04.808 --> 00:01:09.745
climate-smart farming means farming methods that adapt to and reduce climate change.

16
00:01:10.045 --> 00:01:13.171
Climate-smart farming helps farmers cope with drought.

17
00:01:13.871 --> 00:01:17.197
Your turn. Say: climate-smart farming.

18
00:01:19.897 --> 00:01:21.385
climate-smart farming.

19
00:01:22.383 --> 00:01:23.535
soil health.

20
00:01:24.235 --> 00:01:28.220
soil health means the ability of soil to support plants and life.

21
00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:31.077
Too many chemicals damage soil health.

22
00:01:31.777 --> 00:01:35.254
Your turn. Say: soil health.

23
00:01:37.954 --> 00:01:39.233
soil health.

24
00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:41.541
crop rotation.

25
00:01:42.241 --> 00:01:46.574
crop rotation means growing different crops in the same field in turn.

26
00:01:46.874 --> 00:01:49.246
Crop rotation keeps soil fertile.

27
00:01:49.946 --> 00:01:53.109
Your turn. Say: crop rotation.

28
00:01:55.809 --> 00:01:57.042
crop rotation.

29
00:01:58.050 --> 00:01:59.237
agritech.

30
00:01:59.937 --> 00:02:03.272
agritech means technology designed for agriculture.

31
00:02:03.572 --> 00:02:07.324
Cambodian agritech start-ups connect farmers with buyers.

32
00:02:08.024 --> 00:02:10.851
Your turn. Say: agritech.

33
00:02:13.551 --> 00:02:14.645
agritech.

34
00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:17.208
post-harvest loss.

35
00:02:17.908 --> 00:02:22.694
post-harvest loss means food lost after harvesting, during storage or transport.

36
00:02:22.994 --> 00:02:25.934
Post-harvest loss reduces farmers' income.

37
00:02:26.634 --> 00:02:30.320
Your turn. Say: post-harvest loss.

38
00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:34.485
post-harvest loss.

39
00:02:35.483 --> 00:02:36.926
cooperative farming.

40
00:02:37.626 --> 00:02:43.085
cooperative farming means farmers working together to share costs and sell products.

41
00:02:43.385 --> 00:02:47.463
Cooperative farming gives small farmers more bargaining power.

42
00:02:48.163 --> 00:02:51.663
Your turn. Say: cooperative farming.

43
00:02:54.363 --> 00:02:55.689
cooperative farming.

44
00:02:56.683 --> 00:02:58.811
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:59.111 --> 00:03:02.422
Rithy, your family farms in Battambang, doesn't it?

46
00:03:03.717 --> 00:03:09.260
Yes, rice and vegetables. It would seem that farming is changing faster than ever.

47
00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:11.690
In what way?

48
00:03:12.983 --> 00:03:18.608
My cousins use an agritech app to check prices. Arguably, it has increased their income.

49
00:03:19.917 --> 00:03:21.452
And drip irrigation?

50
00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:28.581
It tends to be too expensive for individual farmers, so they share it through cooperative farming.

51
00:03:29.883 --> 00:03:32.478
That's smart. What's the biggest problem?

52
00:03:33.783 --> 00:03:38.874
Post-harvest loss, possibly. A lot of produce spoils before it reaches the market.

53
00:03:40.183 --> 00:03:43.007
Grammar focus: Hedging (mastery).

54
00:03:43.307 --> 00:03:47.095
Mastering hedging makes you sound confident but careful.

55
00:03:47.395 --> 00:03:53.333
It would seem that farming is changing fast. Arguably, the app has increased their income.

56
00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:55.412
It tends to be too expensive.

57
00:03:55.712 --> 00:04:02.402
Mastery of hedging means sounding confident yet careful: never absolute without strong evidence.

58
00:04:03.417 --> 00:04:07.927
Now read and listen. Smart Farms, Strong Communities.

59
00:04:08.227 --> 00:04:12.548
Agriculture employs a large share of Cambodia's workforce.

60
00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:18.624
Climate change, however, appears to be making rainfall less predictable.

61
00:04:19.917 --> 00:04:27.234
Climate-smart farming techniques, such as drip irrigation and crop rotation, may help farmers adapt.

62
00:04:28.550 --> 00:04:33.858
Agritech apps now provide weather forecasts, market prices and farming advice.

63
00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:40.900
Precision agriculture, though still rare, could reduce costs and protect soil health.

64
00:04:42.183 --> 00:04:47.933
Post-harvest loss remains a serious problem, arguably due to poor storage and transport.

65
00:04:49.217 --> 00:04:55.732
Cooperative farming allows small farmers to share equipment and negotiate better prices.

66
00:04:57.017 --> 00:05:01.478
Innovation, it would seem, works best when combined with community cooperation.

67
00:05:02.783 --> 00:05:05.621
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

68
00:05:05.921 --> 00:05:08.943
Watering plants slowly at their roots is blank.

69
00:05:09.243 --> 00:05:14.312
A, drip irrigation. B, crop rotation. C, agritech.

70
00:05:18.317 --> 00:05:20.421
The answer is A: drip irrigation.

71
00:05:21.917 --> 00:05:23.730
Which sentence is hedged?

72
00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:31.283
A, Farming is changing.. B, It would seem that farming is changing.. C, Farming always changes..

73
00:05:35.283 --> 00:05:38.920
The answer is B: It would seem that farming is changing..

74
00:05:40.417 --> 00:05:43.310
This method blank work better in dry areas.

75
00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:47.345
A, tends to. B, tend. C, is tending.

76
00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:53.512
The answer is A: tends to.

77
00:05:55.017 --> 00:05:57.248
Food lost after harvesting is blank.

78
00:05:57.548 --> 00:06:02.850
A, post-harvest loss. B, soil health. C, precision agriculture.

79
00:06:06.850 --> 00:06:09.569
The answer is A: post-harvest loss.

80
00:06:11.083 --> 00:06:15.707
According to the text, what allows small farmers to share equipment?

81
00:06:16.007 --> 00:06:22.029
A, cooperative farming. B, precision agriculture. C, drip irrigation.

82
00:06:26.017 --> 00:06:29.247
The answer is A: cooperative farming.

83
00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:36.212
Now it's your turn. Part one: How could technology help Cambodian farmers?

84
00:06:41.512 --> 00:06:47.343
Part two: Use hedging: suggest two technologies and one limitation.

85
00:06:53.643 --> 00:07:08.105
It would seem that price apps and drip irrigation could help most. Apps arguably give farmers stronger bargaining power, while drip irrigation saves water. However, costs may limit access unless farmers form cooperatives.

86
00:07:08.405 --> 00:07:10.544
That is a well-argued answer!

87
00:07:11.550 --> 00:07:16.188
Great work today! You learned eight new words and hedging (mastery).

88
00:07:16.488 --> 00:07:20.208
Today's value is hard work. Work hard and never give up.

89
00:07:20.508 --> 00:07:23.160
See you in Unit fifty. Goodbye!

90
00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:26.345
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

